  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mission d&apos;evaluation finale des programmes Tien Sira II et Jigiya Kura mise en oeuvre par Association Clinique Juridique Deme-So</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the ToR, an independent evaluation of the TIEN SIRA II (2019-2023, ext. 2024) and Jigiya Kura (2022-2024) programmes is requested by the Dutch Embassy and SIDA. Further consultations emphasized the importance of a strong focus on programme (financial) efficiency, and an in-depth analysis on impact. Based on the OECD criteria, the evaluation will assess how the programmes have performed and delivered on objectives (effectiveness), the significance of that delivery in the current Malian justice context (relevance and impact), and the degree to which they implemented lessons from prior phases and the 2021 Mid-Term Review (relevance). It will also examine the extent to which the two programmes, working in tandem, made optimal use of human and financial resources (efficiency), operated in alignment with each other and other key access to justice programmes and partners (coherence), and the likelihood that achievements continue (sustainability).</narrative>
  </description>
